WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:03.879
- I called the executive
producers over to my house,

00:00:03.962 --> 00:00:07.007
and I told them
that I wanted to come out.

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.968
It became bigger than
any of us ever anticipated.

00:00:12.304 --> 00:00:14.181
- I get a telephone call...

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:16.600
- And my agent sends me this script.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:21.021
- And the character breakdown for the
character of Taylor Mason said non-binary.

00:00:21.104 --> 00:00:22.940
Hello, I'm Taylor.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.150
My pronouns are
"they," "theirs," and "them."

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:31.573
- It's hard to talk about without
stressing how invisible gay people were.

00:00:31.657 --> 00:00:35.953
- The earliest representations
were always people to be mocked.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:38.330
- People couldn't be
just who they were.

00:00:38.413 --> 00:00:42.793
- The truth is, there was no
LGBT presence on TV

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:45.671
that I can remember in 1971.

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:49.508
- We wanted to show people
as they really are.

00:00:49.591 --> 00:00:51.426
- In all that time,
did I ever mention a woman?

00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:55.806
- It's the first time ever on
an American sitcom

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:59.268
that a character came out
and said he was gay.

00:00:59.351 --> 00:01:01.478
- That was, to me,
the breakthrough.

00:01:01.562 --> 00:01:04.189
♪ Clipped wings,
I was a broken thing ♪

00:01:04.273 --> 00:01:07.401
♪ Had a voice, had a voice,
but I could not sing ♪

00:01:07.484 --> 00:01:09.736
♪ You would wind me down ♪

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.697
- We were fighting for our lives.

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:15.075
- I will probably die
before I turn 30 years of age.

00:01:15.158 --> 00:01:18.787
- That's how much homophobia
there is in the community.

00:01:18.871 --> 00:01:22.875
- This was the coming out moment
for the movement on national television.

00:01:22.958 --> 00:01:24.793
This was the time they first saw us.

00:01:25.335 --> 00:01:27.462
- My dad threw me out of the house.

00:01:27.546 --> 00:01:31.675
The episode airs,
and my phone rings...

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:33.343
and it's my dad.

00:01:33.427 --> 00:01:35.888
- One of the great things about television

00:01:35.971 --> 00:01:39.683
is it helps us to make sense of
who we are and where we're going.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:42.895
♪ No, I don't care
if I sing off key ♪

00:01:42.978 --> 00:01:45.063
♪ I find myself in my melodies ♪

00:01:45.147 --> 00:01:46.857
- Something about being on television

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:50.110
makes people see you
as part of our culture.

00:01:50.194 --> 00:01:55.115
- Women who looked like me could be
the centers of their own universe.

00:02:00.287 --> 00:02:04.166
♪ I'll shout it out
like a bird set free ♪

00:02:09.463 --> 00:02:13.717
- When you see images that are
reflective of your own life,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.345
it's a reminder to you
that your life matters.

00:02:17.596 --> 00:02:21.099
- I didn't realize that I was
the revolution that I was waiting for.

00:02:21.183 --> 00:02:24.686
♪ I'll shout it out
like a bird set free ♪

